# Modularity

Follow `docs/architecture/modularity.md`.

## File size (hand-written code only)

| Lines | Action |
|------:|--------|
| < 300 | Ideal for screens, route modules, widgets |
| 300–500 | Acceptable; split when adding features |
| 500–800 | Split on next touch — **CI blocks new files above 500** |
| > 800 | Split immediately |

**CI gate:** `node scripts/check_file_size.js` — fails if any non-grandfathered hand-written `.dart`/`.js` under `flutter_app/lib`, `server/routes` exceeds **500 lines**. Grandfathered paths live in `scripts/file-size-allowlist.json` with a **ratchet ceiling** (must not grow). Remove from allowlist when split below 500.

Exceptions: generated code (`l10n/`, `*.g.dart`, `*.mocks.dart`), lockfiles, canonical SQL.

## Flutter

- No private widget classes > 80 lines inside screen files — move to `widgets/`.
- Controllers own validation, submit, and async orchestration; screens own layout.
- Mirror `lib/features/<feature>/` under `test/features/<feature>/`.

## Backend (Node)

- Route modules live in `server/routes/<domain>/`.
- Tests mirror route modules in `server/test/<domain>/`.
- Mount static paths before `/:id` param routes.

## Refactoring tracking

- Log planned and completed refactor work in `docs/debt/refactoring-log.md` (by sprint).
- Park uncertain items in `docs/debt/refactoring-debt.md`.
